one of the front ones. It made him howl, I can tell you. But just at that moment William came up behind and popped a sack r\r\n\r\n=== text/part0009.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00014.jpeg\r\n  Context: p> “This won’t do at all!” said Thorin. “If we don’t get blown off, or drowned, or struck by lightning, we shall be picked up by some giant and kicked sky-high for a football.” The Mountain-path “Well, if you know of anywhere better, take us there!” said Gandalf, who was feeling very grumpy, and was far from happy about the giants himself. <p class=\"calibre5\"\r\n\r\n=== text/part0011.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00015.jpeg\r\n  Context: dreadful mountains. He was discussing plans with the Great Eagle for carrying the dwarves and himself and Bilbo far away and setting them down well on their journey across the plains below. The Misty Mountains looking West from the Eyrie towards Goblin Gate The Lord of the Eagles would not take them anywhere near where men lived. “They would shoot at us with their great bows of yew\r\n\r\n=== text/part0012.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00016.jpeg\r\n  Context: It faced south and was still warm and filled with the light of the westering sun which slanted into it, and fell golden on the garden full of flowers that came right up to the steps. Here they sat on wooden benches while Gandalf began his tale, and Bilbo swung his dangling legs and looked at the flowers in the garden, wondering what their names could be, as he had never seen half of them be\r\n\r\n=== text/part0014.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00017.jpeg\r\n  Context: wood. On his head was a crown of berries and red leaves, for the autumn was come again. In the spring he wore a crown of woodland flowers. In his hand he held a carven staff of oak. The Elvenking’s Gate The prisoners were brought before him; and though he looked grimly at them, he told his men to unbind them, for they were ragged and weary. “Besides they need no ro\r\n\r\n=== text/part0015.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00018.jpeg\r\n  Context: would flow in rivers, through the mountain-gates, and all that land would be filled with new song and new laughter. But this pleasant legend did not much affect their daily business. As soon as the raft of barrels came in sight boats rowed out from the piles of the town, and voices hailed the raft-steerers. Then ropes were cast and oars were pulled, and soon the raft was drawn out of the current o\r\n\r\n=== text/part0016.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00019.jpeg\r\n  Context: nd again the harsh croak of a bird. Balin shuddered. “Let us return!” he said. “We can do no good here! And I don’t like these dark birds, they look like spies of evil.” The Front Gate. “The dragon is still alive and in the halls under the Mountain then—or I imagine so from the smoke,” said the hobbit. “That does not prove it,” said\r\n\r\n=== text/part0024.html (2 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00020.jpeg\r\n  Context: autumn. And Lake-town was refounded and was more prosperous than ever, and much wealth went up and down the Running River; and there was friendship in those parts between elves and dwarves and men. The Hall at Bag-End Residence of B. Baggins Esquire The old Master had come to a bad end. Bard had given him much gold for the help of the Lake-people, but being of the kind that easily\r\n\r\n  Img: ../images/00021.jpeg\r\n  Context: y fond of you; but you are only quite a little fellow in a wide world after all!” “Thank goodness!” said Bilbo laughing, and handed him the tobacco-jar.\r\n\r\n=== text/part0026.html (1 images) ===\r\n  Img: ../images/00022.jpeg\r\n  Context: /p> Third edition 1966 Fourth edition 1978 Copyright © The J. R. R. Tolkien Copyright Trust 1937, 1951, 1966, 1978, 1995 ® and ‘Tolkien’ ® are registered trademarks of The J. R. R. Tolkien Estate Limited All rights reserved. For informa\r\n\r\n"}
{"step_index":1644,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T07:46:13Z","input_tokens":3657,"cache_read_tokens":121917,"output_tokens":1910,"thinking":"Every image is consistently captioned and positioned within the HTML text. The pattern is clear: each image's filename in the `../images/` directory is referenced alongside its descriptive caption within the corresponding HTML file. This suggests a straightforward method to connect images to their descriptions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import urllib.request, json\n\nproxy_url = \"http://127.0.0.1:20128/v1/chat/completions\"\napi_key = \"sk-2e591994696af18e-71ijj7-14263abd\"\nmodel = \"ag/gemini-3.8-flash\"\n\nsample_text = \"\"\"In a hole in the ground there lived a hobbit. Not a nasty, dirty, wet hole, filled with the ends of worms and an oozy smell, nor yet a dry, bare, sandy hole with nothing in it to sit down on or to eat: it was a hobbit-hole, and that means comfort.\nIt had a perfectly round door like a porthole, painted green, with a shiny yellow brass knob in the exact middle. The door opened on to a tube-shaped hall like a tunnel: a very comfortable tunnel without smoke, with panelled walls, and floors tiled and carpeted, provided with polished chairs, and lots and lots of pegs for hats and coats—the hobbit was fond of visitors.\nThis hobbit was a very well-to-do hobbit, and his name was Baggins. The Bagginses had lived in the neighbourhood of The Hill for time out of mind, and people considered them very respectable, not only because most of them were rich, but also because they never had any adventures or did anything unexpected: you could tell what a Baggins would say on any question without the bother of asking him.\n\n\"Good morning!\" said Bilbo, and he meant it. The sun was shining, and the grass was very green. But Gandalf looked at him from under long bushy eyebrows that stuck out further than the brim of his shady hat.\n\"What do you mean?\" he said. \"Do you wish me a good morning, or mean that it is a good morning whether I want it or not; or that you feel good this morning; or that it is a morning to be good on?\"\n\"All of them at once,\" said Bilbo. \"And a very fine morning for a pipe of tobacco out of doors, into the bargain. If you have a pipe about you, sit down and have a fill of mine! There's no hurry, we have all the day before us!\" Then Bilbo sat down on a seat by his door, crossed his legs, and blew out a beautiful grey ring of smoke that sailed up into the air without breaking and floated away over The Hill.\n\"Very pretty!\" said Gandalf. \"But I have no time to blow smoke-rings this morning. I am looking for someone to share in an adventure that I am arranging, and it's very difficult to find anyone.\"\n\"I should think so — in these parts! We are plain quiet folk and have no use for adventures. Nasty disturbing uncomfortable things! Make you late for dinner! I can't think what anybody sees in them,\" said our Mr. Baggins.\"\"\"\n\nexplanationRule = \"\"\"- Penjelasan Istilah Asing / Teknis / Konsep Dunia Cerita:\n  Setiap istilah asing, istilah teknis, atau konsep yang berpotensi tidak dipahami pembaca dalam narasi maupun dialog harus disertai penjelasan singkat dalam bahasa Indonesia dengan format konsisten: Istilah (arti atau penjelasan sederhana). Contoh: Hobbit (ras manusia kerdil bertelapak kaki tebal berbulu lebat yang anti ribet dan hobi rebahan di lubang tanah super nyaman), Porthole (jendela bundar di kabin kapal).\n  Terapkan secara alami sesuai konteks cerita, tanpa merusak alur, suasana, atau dialog karakter. Jelaskan hanya istilah yang benar-benar berpotensi membingungkan, utamakan saat pertama kali muncul, dan hindari pengulangan penjelasan yang sama. Gunakan bahasa sehari-hari yang lugas, bukan penjelasan formal seperti kamus.\"\"\"\n\nprompt = f\"\"\"Tuliskan seluruh cerita dalam Bahasa Indonesia yang luwes, santai/gaul, hidup, dan to-the-point — setara dengan novel fantasi/petualangan modern terjemahan resmi, webtoon fantasi, atau light novel populer. Target pembaca adalah remaja/young-adult: ritme cepat, ekspresif, adiktif, dan langsung pada pokok masalah. Jangan kaku seperti terjemahan mesin, dan jangan gunakan bahasa formal makalah (\"Anda\", \"mengindikasikan\", \"beliau\"). Format dialog konsisten sertakan Nama: \"...\".\n\nAturan Mutlak:\n- Tell, Don't Show (Lugas & Transparan). Langsung sampaikan situasi, suasana, dan isi pikiran karakter secara tegas.\n- Nol Metafora & Anti-Puitis. Dilarang keras menggunakan kalimat berbunga-bunga lebay.\n- Slang & Percakapan Santai (gue/lu atau gaya bahasa percakapan sehari-hari yang luwes).\n- Format dialog: Nama: \"...\"\n- Pertahankan tag penanda seperti [[ILUSTRASI:...]] persis di posisi adegannya jika ada.\n{explanationRule}\n\nNaskah Mentah:\n{sample_text}\"\"\"\n\npayload = json.dumps({\n    \"model\": model,\n    \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n    \"temperature\": 0.7,\n    \"stream\": False\n}).encode(\"utf-8\")\n\nreq = urllib.request.Request(\n    proxy_url,\n    data=payload,\n    headers={\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n        \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\"\n    }\n)\n\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=60) as resp:\n    result = json.loads(resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\"))\n    print(\"OUTPUT TRANSLATION:\")\n    print(result[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"])\n","Path":"C:\\Users\\Eevyx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\dfaefe40-f699-4276-8717-cb4f8030016c\\scratch\\test_translate_hobbit_sample.py"}}]}
